{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1499 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8392cc40e9a9101312aac12eeaf34165905e7520e08dca628f35a1042a2bfc56" :edb/db-before-t 1498 :edb/db-after-t 1499 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534811 50 #inst "2026-10-12T16:01:03.044Z" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122277 13194139534811 17592186045417 false] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122278 13194139534811 17592186045417 false] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122279 13194139534811 17592186045417 false] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122280 13194139534811 17592186045417 false] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122281 13194139534811 17592186045417 false] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436864 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436870 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436875 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436880 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186122276 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436881 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186122276 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436881 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124440 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436905 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124440 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436907 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124441 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436904 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124441 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436908 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124442 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436906 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124442 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436909 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124726 1050 960.0 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124946 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124946 1071 "Find $g_{xy}(x, y) + g_{xx}(x, y)$ given that $g_{x}(x, y) = \\frac{1}{x - 3y}$." 13194139534811 17592186045417 false] [17592186124946 1071 "Find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)+{g}_{xx}(x,y)$ given that  ${g}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x-3y}.$" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186124946 1074 "To find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{x-3y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(x-3y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{x-3y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(x-3y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y)+{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{3}{(x-3y)^{2}}+(-\\frac{1}{(x-3y)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(x-3y)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186125725 1064 "We can also define other **higher order partial derivatives** such as $f_{xxy}, \\, f_{xxyy}, \\, f_{xyxy},$ etc. \n\nFor instance, the function $f(x,y,z)= z\\cos(xy)$ has the first-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_y(x,y,z) = -xz \\sin(xy)\n$$\n\nand the second-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_{yx}(x,y,z)= -x yz \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} - z\\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIf we differentiate again, with respect to $x,$ then we get the **third-order partial derivative** $f_{yxx}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-xyz\\operatorname{cos}(xy)-z\\operatorname{sin}(xy)) \\\\  & =-yz\\operatorname{cos}(xy)-xyz(-\\operatorname{sin}(xy)\\cdot y)-z\\operatorname{cos}(xy)\\cdot y \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}(xy)-2yz\\operatorname{cos}(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, to compute a $n$th-order partial derivative, we need to compute a sequence of $n$ individual derivatives." 13194139534811 17592186045417 false] [17592186125725 1064 "We can also define other **higher order partial derivatives** such as $f_{xxy}, \\, f_{xxyy}, \\, f_{xyxy},$ etc. \n\nFor instance, the function $f(x,y,z)= z\\cos(xy)$ has the first-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_y(x,y,z) = -xz \\sin(xy)\n$$\n\nand the second-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_{yx}(x,y,z)= -x yz \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} - z\\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIf we differentiate again, with respect to $x,$ then we get the **third-order partial derivative** $f_{yxx}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =-yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xyz(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y)-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\cdot y \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, to compute a $n$th-order partial derivative, we need to compute a sequence of $n$ individual derivatives." 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436863 1080 "\\frac{2}{{e}^{x+2y}}" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436863 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436863 1083 #uuid "0b6c9b46-c3c9-5483-8476-52cbdd59ac4c" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436864 1080 "-\\frac{3}{(x-3y)^{2}}" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436864 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436864 1083 #uuid "0f05c210-c0a0-5abb-b730-98796dd2186c" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436865 1080 "\\frac{3({y}^{2}+2)}{{x}^{4}}" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436865 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436865 1083 #uuid "1121a6b7-cfce-5dfc-b0da-6a636079944b" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436866 1080 "4{e}^{2x}" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436866 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436866 1083 #uuid "11de066d-e9e2-5d24-a361-76b8dd01b39d" 13194139534811 17592186045417 true] [17592186436